  "description": "The unchanged fixedEffects ontology has source and firstEffect at low intensity in world false and high intensity in world true. Necessity, other-directed potential causation and the current-world weak bound hold. Selected-source degree invariance and maximum-at-every-world fail. An attained global maximum nevertheless exists at world true, so this is not a countermodel to existence of some attained maximum or to the unmodeled value/existence bridge. Intensity uses ordered Fin 3 labels independently of ExistsAt, not truth values or numbers of worlds; absent secondEffect intensities are ignored. Worlds are alternatives, not times. This is a singular, other-directed analyst profile, not the entire Koons proof; generic excluded middle is an external logical premise, not certified by this finite interpretation. Formal satisfiability only, no metaphysical possibility or root closure.",
